WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.870 --> 00:00:02.710 align:start position:0%
 
[Applause]  chaos and kiev as thousands jostle at  the train station desperate to leave the  ukrainian capital  soldiers reportedly fired into the air  to disperse the crowd  we've been trying to live all day from  the morning but as you can see that's  unrealistic  russian troops are edging closer with  explosions heard around the city earlier  this apartment block was hit  yes  i was sleeping there was a sharp  explosion and i was thrown three meters  from the room i was in into the corridor  the glass shattered there were sounds  coming from the street i got scared and  started crawling on the floor oksana  gulenko made it out alive while  emergency workers went door to door  searching for victims  and as russian tanks rolled into the  city below ground people crowded into  metro stations exhausted and uncertain  about what's to come  the shelter in our building is not as  far underground as the metro station  that's why i think it's safer to come  down here  at least a hundred thousand people have  been displaced by the fighting  but the united nations says the number  seeking refuge outside ukraine could  reach 5 million  we had to leave behind everything our  whole lives work  it's a terrible feeling to leave your  home you can't imagine how i feel now  these families have crossed the border  into hungary hoping it won't be too long  before they can return  there are long queues at all the banks  and the atms have been emptied there are  throngs in the shops and you pretty much  can't buy anything anymore and even  paying by card is not possible because  some banks are not working and there are  hour long queues at petrol stations  further along the frontier in poland hot  food and drinks are being served with  temperatures hovering around zero  degrees celsius  some people walked 18 hours to get here  many with young children  escaping what rights groups say are  indiscriminate attacks by russian forces  [Music]  ukrainian national anthem as she clears  up after the attack  despite the devastation  an air of defiance remains  alexia o'brien al jazeera

